# villa_wing -- generated by tools/cad/build_shells.py from tools/cad/shells/. DO NOT EDIT.
# the compound's outbuilding wing: 10 x 8, veranda on four posts, hipped roof
# 12.0 x 11.0 m footprint, 5.4 m tall. One piece per material group, all at the
# building's own origin: `tex NAME TILE` is per model file, so a wall and a roof cannot
# share one. The y on each line is the height that group was drawn at, put back: model.c
# rebases every OBJ's lowest vertex to zero, which would otherwise land the roof on the
# ground. Hand-placed extras, if any, follow at the bottom from
# tools/cad/shells/extras/villa_wing.part
piece models/own/shell/villa_wing_floor.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.730 1.910 2.200  tex paving_stone 0.5
piece models/own/shell/villa_wing_wall.obj   0 0.150 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.570 1.740 2.390  tex plaster_cream 0.5
piece models/own/shell/villa_wing_trim.obj   0 0.150 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/shell/villa_wing_roof.obj   0 3.600 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.420 1.530 1.970  tex roof_tile 1.2

# The kit's frames, seated IN the reveals the shell cuts: each piece is pushed back
# into the wall by its own architrave projection, so the moulding finishes flush with
# the plaster instead of standing on it. Generated from the same Walls calls that cut
# the holes, so a frame and its reveal cannot drift apart.
piece models/own/arch/plain_door.obj   0.000 0.150 -3.940   1.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.470 1.250 0.880  tex planks_weathered 2.5
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   -3.000 0.950 -3.930   1.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   3.000 0.950 -3.930   1.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   -0.000 0.950 3.930   1.000 1.000 1.000   180.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   -4.930 0.950 -0.000   1.000 1.000 1.000   90.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/window_small.obj   4.930 0.950 0.000   1.000 1.000 1.000   -90.0 0.0 0.0   1.670 1.730 1.830  tex plaster_smooth 0.8

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/villa_wing.part ----
# Nothing hand-placed here: the old villa_wing.part had no air conditioner, washing line or
# other prop beyond its fabric, so there is nothing to carry over.

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/villa_wing_facade.part ----
# The old wing_facade.part's wall_column veranda posts and cornice_run/roof_edge_run trim are
# superseded here: villa.py's villa_wing() models the veranda posts, head beam and eave course
# as real CAD geometry (the way cabana.py's porch does it) rather than dressing thin placeholder
# cylinders with kit pieces, so nothing from the old facade needs to be hand-carried across.
